WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:09.009
[♪ epic theme music playing]

2
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:17.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

3
00:01:56.575 --> 00:01:58.577
[birdsong]

4
00:02:06.585 --> 00:02:09.588
[♪ dramatic music playing]

5
00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:18.430
Tully's been here.

6
00:02:19.681 --> 00:02:22.267
We found one of their camps
just ahead.

7
00:02:23.518 --> 00:02:26.605
But something...
strange has happened there.

8
00:02:56.343 --> 00:02:58.345
[insects buzzing]

9
00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:06.228
They're all Rivermen.

10
00:03:08.313 --> 00:03:09.356
Who killed them?

11
00:03:10.649 --> 00:03:12.317
We found no sign of their foe.

12
00:03:29.918 --> 00:03:31.503
They did not fall here.

13
00:03:38.009 --> 00:03:39.678
[shouting]
On your guard!

14
00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.471
It's a trap!

15
00:03:41.513 --> 00:03:44.516
[all shouting. grunting]

16
00:03:55.402 --> 00:03:57.195
-[choking]
-To me!

17
00:04:12.711 --> 00:04:14.087
[shouting]

18
00:04:15.589 --> 00:04:16.757
Aaah!

19
00:04:19.134 --> 00:04:20.135
[grunts]

20
00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:23.221
Ah!

21
00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:29.895
[shouting]

22
00:04:32.397 --> 00:04:34.316
[swords clanging]

23
00:04:40.906 --> 00:04:43.241
[swords clanging]

24
00:04:54.753 --> 00:04:55.753
Yah!

25
00:04:59.257 --> 00:05:01.259
[groaning]

26
00:05:03.261 --> 00:05:05.263
[panting]

27
00:05:10.769 --> 00:05:12.270
We light the way!

28
00:05:12.312 --> 00:05:15.273
[all shouting]
We light the way!

29
00:05:16.817 --> 00:05:18.610
[banging]

30
00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:25.283
[slow. repetitive banging
continues]

31
00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:35.627
This was not the battle.

32
00:05:35.669 --> 00:05:37.671
[slow. repetitive banging
continues]

33
00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:44.970
Who are they?

34
00:05:45.971 --> 00:05:47.973
-Our death.
-[banging continues]

35
00:05:50.976 --> 00:05:52.477
[Oscar Tully]
Criston Cole!

36
00:05:54.688 --> 00:05:59.109
Traitor. usurper.
and defiler of justice.

37
00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:00.944
Come forth to hear your fate.

38
00:06:00.986 --> 00:06:04.614
If I strike my banners.
will you spare my men their lives?

39
00:06:04.656 --> 00:06:08.034
-[chuckles]
-I made a promise to the dead. Cole.

40
00:06:08.076 --> 00:06:10.662
I told them I'd build a sept
out of traitors' bones.

41
00:06:11.538 --> 00:06:13.331
I don't have
near enough bones yet.

42
00:06:15.083 --> 00:06:16.084
Hm.

43
00:06:21.882 --> 00:06:25.302
If there is to be battle here.
many of you will die as well.

44
00:06:25.343 --> 00:06:26.802
That's why we've come.

45
00:06:26.803 --> 00:06:30.682
What better way to die
than blade in hand?

46
00:06:34.936 --> 00:06:36.354
As you will it.

47
00:06:43.737 --> 00:06:47.073
[♪ somber music playing]

48
00:06:55.707 --> 00:06:57.542
Let us begin here then.

49
00:06:59.544 --> 00:07:01.338
One of me
against the two of you.

50
00:07:01.379 --> 00:07:02.547
[groaning softly]

51
00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:06.426
Will that be enough
to make a fight of it?

52
00:07:08.553 --> 00:07:09.804
[arrow thwacking]

53
00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:13.725
[arrow thwacking]

54
00:07:20.732 --> 00:07:22.734
♪♪

55
00:07:35.622 --> 00:07:38.416
[soldiers shouting]

56
00:07:42.128 --> 00:07:45.131
[♪ somber music
continues playing]

57
00:07:49.594 --> 00:07:52.597
♪♪

58
00:08:07.278 --> 00:08:08.613
[guard]
They're here.

59
00:08:10.448 --> 00:08:11.866
[sighs]

60
00:08:19.457 --> 00:08:22.502
I mourn my friend Ser Luthor.

61
00:08:22.544 --> 00:08:25.171
and some four and 10
of his best men.

62
00:08:25.213 --> 00:08:26.857
A total count of five and 20
of the City Watch

63
00:08:26.881 --> 00:08:28.717
now slain in the name
of "King Daeron."

64
00:08:29.718 --> 00:08:33.179
Lord Ormund mocks us
in our own city.

65
00:08:33.221 --> 00:08:34.806
He means to show the realm

66
00:08:34.848 --> 00:08:38.101
that I cannot govern
even my own seat.

67
00:08:38.143 --> 00:08:41.312
The great houses watch
while he humiliates me.

68
00:08:41.354 --> 00:08:43.273
Where is my army?

69
00:08:43.314 --> 00:08:44.983
Ser Criston has hindered them.

70
00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:48.987
The vanguard is still
a fortnight's march from Tumbleton.

71
00:08:49.029 --> 00:08:50.363
The insult must be answered now.

72
00:08:50.405 --> 00:08:51.799
We must do what we
should have done in the first.

73
00:08:51.823 --> 00:08:53.450
Burn the villains out.

74
00:08:53.491 --> 00:08:55.702
Then Ormund gets what he wants.

75
00:08:55.744 --> 00:08:58.663
A queen who murders
loyal subjects cannot be trusted.

76
00:08:58.705 --> 00:09:00.558
We know where the traitor
has entrenched himself.

77
00:09:00.582 --> 00:09:03.209
If I fly directly
to the Footly stronghold...

78
00:09:03.251 --> 00:09:05.045
[Lady Sabitha]
On a dragon. I presume.

79
00:09:05.086 --> 00:09:07.130
A beast well known
for its delicacy

80
00:09:07.172 --> 00:09:09.007
and precision in battle.

81
00:09:09.049 --> 00:09:10.884
Ah. yes. what a marvel.

82
00:09:10.925 --> 00:09:13.470
The flame it spews forth
can discern with pure magic

83
00:09:13.511 --> 00:09:15.138
who is blameless
and who is deserving...

84
00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:16.723
[metal clanging]

85
00:09:17.307 --> 00:09:19.476
I'll hear no more from those
whose greatest battle

86
00:09:19.517 --> 00:09:20.809
has been
with their own indigestion.

87
00:09:20.810 --> 00:09:22.979
[Alyn]
I am of the same mind as the lord

88
00:09:23.021 --> 00:09:24.898
and ladies. Your Grace.

89
00:09:24.939 --> 00:09:27.025
Your army marches ever nearer.

90
00:09:28.526 --> 00:09:30.904
You will answer
this outrage with force

91
00:09:30.945 --> 00:09:33.031
but discriminately...

92
00:09:35.825 --> 00:09:38.185
-if we wait but a while longer.
-[Daemon] At what cost?

93
00:09:38.953 --> 00:09:41.164
Remember the prophecy.
your sacred calling.

94
00:09:41.206 --> 00:09:43.583
Whatever you do in its service
is justified.

95
00:09:43.625 --> 00:09:45.043
Aegon the Conqueror
burned thousands

96
00:09:45.085 --> 00:09:46.669
on the Field of Fire. thousands.

97
00:09:46.711 --> 00:09:48.022
and settled the realm
for generations...

98
00:09:48.046 --> 00:09:49.380
The Conqueror

99
00:09:49.422 --> 00:09:51.442
burned enemy soldiers.
not subjects who bent the knee.

100
00:09:51.466 --> 00:09:53.551
Their lord bent the knee to you!

101
00:09:54.511 --> 00:09:56.387
The people would just
as happily follow a mule

102
00:09:56.429 --> 00:09:58.348
-if that same...
-My father would abhor it.

103
00:09:58.389 --> 00:10:00.266
Ah. and there we have it.

104
00:10:01.893 --> 00:10:02.894
But...

105
00:10:04.104 --> 00:10:06.606
my patience has its bounds.

106
00:10:06.648 --> 00:10:08.608
-I will send knives.
-[Daemon] So be it.

107
00:10:08.650 --> 00:10:11.212
At least I will get to meet
the fiend face-to-face before he dies.

108
00:10:11.236 --> 00:10:12.403
Oh. no. not you.

109
00:10:14.489 --> 00:10:16.074
I will have my satisfaction.

110
00:10:17.742 --> 00:10:18.827
Yes.

111
00:10:19.661 --> 00:10:21.913
But the most effective assassin
has a plain face.

112
00:10:23.623 --> 00:10:25.875
Fanatics still prowl the streets

113
00:10:25.917 --> 00:10:28.753
outside our castle gates
at Lord Ormund's bidding.

114
00:10:28.795 --> 00:10:30.505
That is your charge.

115
00:10:34.092 --> 00:10:35.885
Your Grace. there is
a detachment left here

116
00:10:35.927 --> 00:10:37.262
of Velaryon men. soldiers.

117
00:10:37.303 --> 00:10:39.097
ready to aid
Prince Daemon in his...

118
00:10:39.139 --> 00:10:40.598
I think not.

119
00:10:45.061 --> 00:10:48.731
How many Velaryon men
remain in King's Landing?

120
00:10:48.773 --> 00:10:50.400
Some threescore. Your Grace.

121
00:10:50.441 --> 00:10:52.402
Petition your father for more.

122
00:10:52.443 --> 00:10:54.737
They may be needed
to secure the city.

123
00:10:54.779 --> 00:10:56.948
Who then will you send
to Tumbleton?

124
00:10:57.949 --> 00:11:01.619
It is a dangerous errand.
and one that will require force.

125
00:11:03.454 --> 00:11:06.875
[Ser Lyonel] My queen. the delegation
from House Baratheon has arrived.

126
00:11:08.918 --> 00:11:13.173
Your Grace. I am sent
to represent House Baratheon

127
00:11:13.214 --> 00:11:14.632
in response to your summons.

128
00:11:16.843 --> 00:11:18.094
Where is Lord Borros?

129
00:11:18.136 --> 00:11:20.430
Lord Borros begs patience.
my queen.

130
00:11:20.471 --> 00:11:22.348
He has taken his army
to the Red Mountains

131
00:11:22.390 --> 00:11:23.850
to fight the Vulture King.

132
00:11:23.892 --> 00:11:26.769
who has been raiding
the Stormlands these many moons.

133
00:11:26.811 --> 00:11:28.813
His queen summons him north.

134
00:11:28.855 --> 00:11:31.858
and all of a sudden it occurs
to him that he must ride south.

135
00:11:33.026 --> 00:11:35.111
It is my lord's duty

136
00:11:35.153 --> 00:11:37.447
to guard the realm
against the Dornish threat.

137
00:11:37.488 --> 00:11:39.282
As it was his duty
to guard my son

138
00:11:39.324 --> 00:11:41.826
when he came to treat
with him beneath his roof?

139
00:11:43.036 --> 00:11:45.038
Once the Vulture King
has been subdued...

140
00:11:45.079 --> 00:11:47.956
Your lord makes the mistake
of considering a common bandit

141
00:11:47.957 --> 00:11:50.668
a greater threat
to his interests than I am.

142
00:11:53.421 --> 00:11:57.008
I could brand him a traitor
and hang you in his stead.

143
00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:02.639
No disrespect was intended.
Your Grace.

144
00:12:02.680 --> 00:12:04.015
to you or your endeavors.

145
00:12:04.057 --> 00:12:06.809
It is but... but a matter
of time.

146
00:12:06.851 --> 00:12:08.144
Time?

147
00:12:08.728 --> 00:12:12.398
If there were aught else
I could offer you at this moment.

148
00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:14.567
I would lay it before you
most willingly.

149
00:12:20.531 --> 00:12:21.866
Give me your belt.

150
00:12:22.867 --> 00:12:24.827
[Vermithor bellowing]

151
00:12:24.869 --> 00:12:26.829
[people chattering]

152
00:12:26.871 --> 00:12:29.874
[♪ dramatic music playing]

153
00:12:39.759 --> 00:12:41.761
[chittering]

154
00:12:47.725 --> 00:12:50.728
[dragons chittering]

155
00:12:54.399 --> 00:12:55.566
Anything to report?

156
00:12:58.486 --> 00:12:59.737
[chuckles softly]

157
00:13:01.781 --> 00:13:03.199
Market day tomorrow.

158
00:13:03.241 --> 00:13:05.001
Do you remember Market Day
in King's Landing?

159
00:13:06.744 --> 00:13:07.912
Before all of this?

160
00:13:07.954 --> 00:13:09.956
[dragons continue chittering]

161
00:13:11.332 --> 00:13:12.625
Fruit stalls.

162
00:13:14.294 --> 00:13:16.462
Geese honking.
Traders shouting.

163
00:13:17.755 --> 00:13:19.674
[sighs] Hot pies.

164
00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:25.388
Took it all for granted.
didn't we?

165
00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:27.765
It will soon be
the same again. I imagine.

166
00:13:27.807 --> 00:13:30.059
But we're not the same. are we?

167
00:13:30.101 --> 00:13:31.936
We weren't in service back then.

168
00:13:33.646 --> 00:13:35.732
At the beck and call
of the queen

169
00:13:35.773 --> 00:13:38.776
sleeping on a hill... alone.

170
00:13:40.862 --> 00:13:43.239
She stopped me
going to the tavern. Hugh.

171
00:13:43.281 --> 00:13:44.991
Not one ale with the lads.

172
00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:47.410
What's the point
in having a dragon

173
00:13:47.452 --> 00:13:48.828
if no one's around to see it?

174
00:13:51.372 --> 00:13:53.624
Well. would you go back
to where you were?

175
00:13:53.666 --> 00:13:55.793
Scrabbling around in the dust?

176
00:13:57.295 --> 00:13:59.213
-No.
-Mm.

177
00:14:01.591 --> 00:14:03.885
Though I can't say my life
has been improved.

178
00:14:06.095 --> 00:14:07.305
Can you?

179
00:14:09.974 --> 00:14:11.309
[scoffs lightly]

180
00:14:13.519 --> 00:14:15.646
Right. then. [grunting]

181
00:14:21.069 --> 00:14:23.654
[sighs] See you in two days.

182
00:14:25.406 --> 00:14:26.657
Ser Hugh.

183
00:14:29.452 --> 00:14:31.204
[whistling] Come on. girl.

184
00:14:41.839 --> 00:14:43.341
[door opens]

185
00:14:46.886 --> 00:14:48.054
Leave us.

186
00:14:53.768 --> 00:14:55.019
You would have done the same.

187
00:14:56.229 --> 00:14:58.648
Have I not shown you mercy

188
00:14:58.689 --> 00:15:02.568
even before those who named
my kindness to you a weakness?

189
00:15:02.610 --> 00:15:04.404
Are you so ungrateful

190
00:15:04.445 --> 00:15:06.614
-that you insist upon...
-Helaena is with child.

191
00:15:11.577 --> 00:15:13.871
So. you flee.

192
00:15:14.747 --> 00:15:17.542
To preserve the babe's life.
and Helaena's with it.

193
00:15:17.583 --> 00:15:19.961
[scoffs] Still you insist
on misjudging me.

194
00:15:21.045 --> 00:15:23.172
If the child is male.

195
00:15:23.214 --> 00:15:25.049
would you not in the end
find it necessary?

196
00:15:27.552 --> 00:15:29.220
To hold him hostage.
at the least?

197
00:15:30.763 --> 00:15:32.306
To draw out Aemond or...

198
00:15:33.224 --> 00:15:34.725
or Ormund in his pride?

199
00:15:36.602 --> 00:15:39.605
Or simply to secure
your own reign from endless challenges.

200
00:15:39.647 --> 00:15:41.983
You were discovered by guards.

201
00:15:44.986 --> 00:15:47.196
I cannot let this go unanswered.

202
00:15:47.238 --> 00:15:48.865
Helaena did
as I persuaded her to do.

203
00:15:48.906 --> 00:15:51.117
If you must be cruel.
let it be me who suffers.

204
00:15:51.159 --> 00:15:52.326
Only spare her.

205
00:15:53.453 --> 00:15:55.580
You must both now
be more strictly confined.

206
00:15:56.247 --> 00:15:58.082
Your guard is doubled.

207
00:15:58.124 --> 00:16:00.418
There'll be no more walks
in the Godswood.

208
00:16:00.460 --> 00:16:02.229
-I accept this judgment for myself...
-My judgment

209
00:16:02.253 --> 00:16:04.046
does not require
your acceptance.

210
00:16:04.088 --> 00:16:05.798
Rhaenyra. you know what she is.

211
00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:08.092
She is fragile.
you... you cannot confine her.

212
00:16:08.134 --> 00:16:09.719
I didn't!

213
00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:11.679
And now. I must!

214
00:16:12.930 --> 00:16:14.974
She cannot be seen.

215
00:16:15.016 --> 00:16:16.642
If she is known
to carry Aegon's heir.

216
00:16:16.684 --> 00:16:18.436
I will be forced to do
what you fear.

217
00:16:18.478 --> 00:16:21.063
Well. so. so. so send us
away then to some remote...

218
00:16:21.105 --> 00:16:23.483
Away? Now?

219
00:16:24.775 --> 00:16:26.068
Your son is still at liberty.

220
00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:28.821
Your cousin wreaks chaos
within my city walls.

221
00:16:30.156 --> 00:16:32.950
Even today. I must answer
another of his murderous treasons.

222
00:16:35.286 --> 00:16:37.079
You are a Hightower.

223
00:16:37.121 --> 00:16:38.706
To my court. you are the enemy.

224
00:16:39.665 --> 00:16:40.833
And to you?

225
00:16:43.336 --> 00:16:44.545
Do not try me.

226
00:16:47.131 --> 00:16:48.966
-[sighs]
-[door opens]

227
00:16:50.968 --> 00:16:52.470
What did she tell you?

228
00:16:53.804 --> 00:16:55.556
Helaena is with child.

229
00:16:57.975 --> 00:16:59.644
Are there others who know?

230
00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:02.396
I believe not.

231
00:17:03.314 --> 00:17:04.857
You yourself had no suspicion?

232
00:17:05.816 --> 00:17:06.817
No.

233
00:17:08.027 --> 00:17:09.153
No.

234
00:17:09.195 --> 00:17:11.197
♪♪

235
00:17:20.164 --> 00:17:21.832
That one.

236
00:17:21.874 --> 00:17:23.834
A thief and a liar.

237
00:17:25.836 --> 00:17:27.547
Let me know when it's done.

238
00:17:44.939 --> 00:17:46.524
We will be avenged.

239
00:17:49.026 --> 00:17:50.861
If it takes a hundred years.

240
00:18:00.871 --> 00:18:02.206
What's this?

241
00:18:05.710 --> 00:18:08.004
Forgive me. my prince.

242
00:18:08.045 --> 00:18:09.714
This is how you answer?

243
00:18:11.632 --> 00:18:12.717
With desertion?

244
00:18:12.758 --> 00:18:15.011
The queen asked for loyalty.

245
00:18:15.052 --> 00:18:16.887
and I was willing enough
to wait.

246
00:18:18.389 --> 00:18:20.558
But my children
are now penniless.

247
00:18:22.101 --> 00:18:24.020
I will not leave them
fatherless as well.

248
00:18:24.061 --> 00:18:26.856
Small wonder Hightower vermin
swarm our streets

249
00:18:26.897 --> 00:18:29.775
when they smell
your craven stink.

250
00:18:29.817 --> 00:18:32.612
My first duty
must be to my family.

251
00:18:33.738 --> 00:18:36.240
I-I will earn our coin
another way.

252
00:18:36.282 --> 00:18:38.784
And when cutthroats
and scoundrels swarm your house.

253
00:18:38.826 --> 00:18:40.786
rip the bread
from your children's mouths.

254
00:18:40.828 --> 00:18:43.247
and take their pleasure
with your wife.

255
00:18:45.666 --> 00:18:46.959
All of you.

256
00:18:49.086 --> 00:18:51.005
You forget what this city was!

257
00:18:52.757 --> 00:18:55.718
Before I turned this rabble
into an army.

258
00:18:55.760 --> 00:18:57.470
before I led you
out of your squalor

259
00:18:57.511 --> 00:18:58.929
and formed you into men!

260
00:19:02.642 --> 00:19:03.643
[whispering] Shame.

261
00:19:12.693 --> 00:19:15.696
[♪ dramatic music playing]

262
00:19:31.671 --> 00:19:33.673
[people chattering]

263
00:19:35.383 --> 00:19:37.677
Word in the city is that
you've done valiant work.

264
00:19:38.844 --> 00:19:40.471
The Triarchy raids
have dwindled.

265
00:19:42.056 --> 00:19:43.307
There's more to do.

266
00:19:44.975 --> 00:19:46.560
As ever will be the case.

267
00:19:48.396 --> 00:19:49.855
State your purpose. Alyn.

268
00:19:49.897 --> 00:19:53.275
Ormund Hightower strikes
insidiously at King's Landing.

269
00:19:53.317 --> 00:19:54.819
seeking to throw it into chaos.

270
00:19:55.695 --> 00:19:57.779
The City Watch is buckling.

271
00:19:57.780 --> 00:19:59.365
I would send to Driftmark

272
00:19:59.407 --> 00:20:01.287
to shore up their number
with good Velaryon men.

273
00:20:01.325 --> 00:20:03.369
So. she asks more of me.

274
00:20:05.496 --> 00:20:07.665
It is I who ask.

275
00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:13.003
Do as you have said.
Her needs are endless.

276
00:20:14.672 --> 00:20:17.299
Have you not exhausted
your anger yet?

277
00:20:17.341 --> 00:20:18.843
You take her side...

278
00:20:19.885 --> 00:20:22.471
when she yet refuses
to grant you legitimacy.

279
00:20:22.513 --> 00:20:26.016
And how many years did it
take you to do the same?

280
00:20:32.106 --> 00:20:33.607
I have heard things...

281
00:20:35.401 --> 00:20:37.695
in questioning these pirates.

282
00:20:39.363 --> 00:20:41.907
Tell her Tyland Lannister
survived the Gullet...

283
00:20:43.868 --> 00:20:45.536
and is making for Rook's Rest.

284
00:20:54.754 --> 00:20:56.756
[shovel digging]

285
00:20:58.257 --> 00:21:00.259
[grunting]

286
00:21:03.888 --> 00:21:06.265
-That's enough.
-The dogs will find him.

287
00:21:07.558 --> 00:21:08.893
They're welcome to him.

288
00:21:08.934 --> 00:21:10.519
By the time they come.
we'll be gone.

289
00:21:10.561 --> 00:21:12.563
But not far.
And if the others realize...

290
00:21:12.605 --> 00:21:15.065
If you wish to dig deeper.
Lord Larys.

291
00:21:15.107 --> 00:21:16.734
the shovel is free.

292
00:21:27.745 --> 00:21:29.205
I have found passage to Braavos

293
00:21:29.246 --> 00:21:31.165
on a merchant cog
out of Maidenpool.

294
00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:35.377
We must draw as little notice
as we can for a few days

295
00:21:35.419 --> 00:21:37.171
as we provision ourselves.
but...

296
00:21:39.131 --> 00:21:41.258
I believe we can sail
before the full moon.

297
00:21:42.259 --> 00:21:44.011
I must interject. my king.

298
00:21:45.095 --> 00:21:47.431
I still feel
it would be an error

299
00:21:47.473 --> 00:21:48.808
for you to leave Westeros.

300
00:21:50.434 --> 00:21:53.103
You would be best served
at Casterly Rock.

301
00:21:53.145 --> 00:21:54.605
where we can establish a court

302
00:21:54.647 --> 00:21:56.106
and enjoin those
still loyal to you.

303
00:21:56.148 --> 00:22:00.194
Do you think
I'm a terrible man. Ser Tyland?

304
00:22:03.697 --> 00:22:04.990
I would never say...

305
00:22:06.283 --> 00:22:08.494
That is...

306
00:22:08.536 --> 00:22:11.163
while I may not have always
agreed with every course of...

307
00:22:12.790 --> 00:22:14.291
Um. well...

308
00:22:15.209 --> 00:22:16.210
[Tyland stammering]

309
00:22:17.461 --> 00:22:18.462
There is...

310
00:22:19.797 --> 00:22:22.258
in any one of us. I venture...

311
00:22:23.342 --> 00:22:26.554
much to admire
and much to be deplored.

312
00:22:29.807 --> 00:22:31.809
[clicking tongue. sighs]

313
00:22:36.647 --> 00:22:37.648
Mm.

314
00:22:40.192 --> 00:22:41.819
We sail for Essos. then.

315
00:22:44.405 --> 00:22:47.408
[♪ dramatic music playing]

316
00:22:50.327 --> 00:22:52.663
[wind whistling]

317
00:22:56.166 --> 00:22:58.335
[Sheepstealer calls]

318
00:23:01.589 --> 00:23:03.591
[dragon shrieks]

319
00:23:12.266 --> 00:23:14.268
[dragon chirping]

320
00:23:27.531 --> 00:23:28.741
For your face.

321
00:23:35.456 --> 00:23:38.042
It's been long since anyone
sought to defend me.

322
00:23:40.127 --> 00:23:41.921
I am in your debt.

323
00:23:43.464 --> 00:23:46.175
As I am apparently in yours.

324
00:23:46.216 --> 00:23:48.928
But I'm glad I can leave here
now with that score settled.

325
00:23:52.014 --> 00:23:54.058
Where do you think to go?

326
00:23:54.099 --> 00:23:55.601
I need to find my dragon.

327
00:23:56.602 --> 00:23:58.938
She would not have
left me willingly.

328
00:23:58.979 --> 00:24:00.481
and I'll not be without her.

329
00:24:04.068 --> 00:24:06.278
A frog in winter
sleeps under the ice.

330
00:24:07.237 --> 00:24:08.781
Still and silent.

331
00:24:10.658 --> 00:24:11.825
Mend your wounds.

332
00:24:13.077 --> 00:24:14.411
Gather your strength.

333
00:24:15.788 --> 00:24:18.082
Let the world think you dead

334
00:24:18.123 --> 00:24:20.125
until the spring thaw.

335
00:24:21.835 --> 00:24:23.170
I need to find a horse.

336
00:24:24.171 --> 00:24:25.798
To ride where?

337
00:24:26.715 --> 00:24:28.610
Over the numberless leagues
of the Seven Kingdoms?

338
00:24:28.634 --> 00:24:30.469
Vhagar will come to me.

339
00:24:30.511 --> 00:24:33.097
It is perhaps this forsaken
castle she shuns.

340
00:24:33.138 --> 00:24:36.392
Or if not.
I'll go to King's Landing.

341
00:24:36.433 --> 00:24:38.286
It's said she haunted
the hills outside the city

342
00:24:38.310 --> 00:24:40.062
in the years before I was born.

343
00:24:40.104 --> 00:24:41.939
There is a bounty on your life.

344
00:24:44.149 --> 00:24:46.944
Every sellsword
is combing the woods

345
00:24:46.986 --> 00:24:49.321
hoping to slit your throat
in the night.

346
00:24:51.115 --> 00:24:52.950
Oh. and half
the commonfolk. too.

347
00:24:55.786 --> 00:24:57.621
Even you must sleep.

348
00:24:59.623 --> 00:25:01.959
There's no place for you
to rest your head.

349
00:25:03.210 --> 00:25:04.837
And nor am I safe here then.

350
00:25:06.547 --> 00:25:09.008
Or you. for harboring me.

351
00:25:10.718 --> 00:25:13.012
Is it possible that Vhagar
flew away

352
00:25:13.053 --> 00:25:15.848
as a way of protecting you?

353
00:25:18.642 --> 00:25:20.310
Without her. you're hidden.

354
00:25:22.479 --> 00:25:25.065
The queen assumes that
where your dragon is...

355
00:25:27.151 --> 00:25:28.819
there you will be. too.

356
00:25:33.824 --> 00:25:35.492
She is no queen.

357
00:25:35.534 --> 00:25:39.371
And when you find your mount.
will you fly to your death?

358
00:25:41.206 --> 00:25:43.500
Rhaenyra has six dragons
to your one.

359
00:25:44.835 --> 00:25:47.129
You'll fall alone.

360
00:25:47.171 --> 00:25:48.505
And to what end?

361
00:25:51.050 --> 00:25:53.052
[person screaming]

362
00:25:55.179 --> 00:25:56.889
Never ceases to be fascinating.

363
00:25:59.850 --> 00:26:01.393
[door opens]

364
00:26:06.690 --> 00:26:08.108
As you ordered. my lady.

365
00:26:21.747 --> 00:26:23.540
What did I say.
when last we met?

366
00:26:25.417 --> 00:26:26.877
I saw Moondancer...

367
00:26:28.045 --> 00:26:31.673
my sister's dragon.
flying towards Iron Oaks.

368
00:26:31.715 --> 00:26:33.217
And what does that
to do with you?

369
00:26:34.218 --> 00:26:36.136
She's my sister. I...

370
00:26:37.221 --> 00:26:39.264
I thought if I could
just see her face.

371
00:26:39.306 --> 00:26:42.726
So you leave your hiding place.
in violation of our agreement.

372
00:26:42.768 --> 00:26:46.230
and you fly toward a town equipped
with several thousand pairs of eyes.

373
00:26:46.271 --> 00:26:49.441
all watching and wondering
what your appearance portends.

374
00:26:49.483 --> 00:26:51.568
I didn't even see her.
She was already gone.

375
00:26:51.610 --> 00:26:53.810
And what do you think
would have happened if she hadn't?

376
00:26:57.282 --> 00:26:59.868
The queen thinks
Sheepstealer's rider is dead.

377
00:26:59.910 --> 00:27:01.453
It has been your only reprieve.

378
00:27:01.495 --> 00:27:02.913
If word reaches her...

379
00:27:05.749 --> 00:27:08.293
Have you forgotten already
the doom that hangs over you?

380
00:27:10.963 --> 00:27:12.256
And over me.

381
00:27:13.757 --> 00:27:15.092
For harboring you.

382
00:27:16.927 --> 00:27:19.012
For allowing myself
to be swayed.

383
00:27:20.347 --> 00:27:22.599
-I'm sorry.
-Mm.

384
00:27:22.641 --> 00:27:26.270
All my life.
I have yearned after a dragon.

385
00:27:28.480 --> 00:27:31.275
And now I have one.
but I have lost everything else.

386
00:27:33.527 --> 00:27:34.820
That was your choice.

387
00:27:36.113 --> 00:27:37.531
They are dead to you now.

388
00:27:38.615 --> 00:27:41.535
But you got
what you wanted. Go.

389
00:27:42.786 --> 00:27:44.872
And the next time
you try me will be the last.

390
00:27:47.541 --> 00:27:49.543
[dragon screeching. bellowing]

391
00:27:55.132 --> 00:27:56.842
A bed would be more comfortable.

392
00:27:59.511 --> 00:28:00.637
My lady.

393
00:28:02.723 --> 00:28:03.849
I'm going.

394
00:28:04.808 --> 00:28:06.935
I just needed
a little more time.

395
00:28:06.977 --> 00:28:10.022
I know what it is
to be so weary.

396
00:28:11.523 --> 00:28:13.275
[clearing throat]

397
00:28:13.317 --> 00:28:16.653
I. uh... saw my father today.

398
00:28:19.531 --> 00:28:21.533
I was wondering
if you would speak to him.

399
00:28:24.036 --> 00:28:26.288
There is a distance there.

400
00:28:26.330 --> 00:28:28.165
as if he's removed
himself entirely.

401
00:28:29.541 --> 00:28:30.751
I just thought...

402
00:28:32.211 --> 00:28:35.255
maybe now he might. um...

403
00:28:37.216 --> 00:28:38.383
see me.

404
00:28:41.178 --> 00:28:42.763
I thought the same
with my father.

405
00:28:44.723 --> 00:28:49.019
They cannot face their ghosts.
so they seek to outstrip them.

406
00:28:50.562 --> 00:28:52.189
Even if they leave us behind.

407
00:28:54.107 --> 00:28:58.528
They roam. they punish.
they fight. they do.

408
00:29:00.280 --> 00:29:01.740
[sighs]

409
00:29:02.741 --> 00:29:04.201
I cannot help him. Alyn.

410
00:29:05.702 --> 00:29:07.871
I have my own burdens to bear.

411
00:29:22.678 --> 00:29:25.305
I. uh... [clearing throat]
You should go to bed.

412
00:29:39.403 --> 00:29:40.904
You're very dutiful.

413
00:29:45.909 --> 00:29:47.160
I am the eldest.

414
00:29:49.454 --> 00:29:51.081
It must get wearisome...

415
00:29:52.499 --> 00:29:54.668
attending to everyone else
all the time.

416
00:29:58.422 --> 00:29:59.756
Maybe a little.

417
00:30:02.843 --> 00:30:04.678
Don't you ever want
to forget it all?

418
00:30:06.430 --> 00:30:07.931
Do what you want?

419
00:30:10.267 --> 00:30:13.270
[♪ gentle music playing]

420
00:30:32.622 --> 00:30:37.794
And so. Ser Criston fights on.
and yet you have returned.

421
00:30:37.836 --> 00:30:38.837
Because...

422
00:30:40.172 --> 00:30:42.132
Because fighting on is madness.

423
00:30:45.802 --> 00:30:48.263
Do you think me mad. Your Grace?

424
00:30:48.305 --> 00:30:50.349
No. sire.

425
00:30:50.390 --> 00:30:51.391
Hm.

426
00:30:52.351 --> 00:30:53.810
[Gwayne]
You mean to fight on?

427
00:30:54.728 --> 00:30:56.605
With what?

428
00:30:56.646 --> 00:30:58.815
There's a dragon
sitting on the hill above us.

429
00:30:58.857 --> 00:31:00.609
and five more
not 30 leagues away.

430
00:31:00.650 --> 00:31:03.779
Rhaenyra will not burn
her own subjects.

431
00:31:03.820 --> 00:31:05.197
She is a woman.

432
00:31:06.365 --> 00:31:07.866
Squeamish.

433
00:31:07.908 --> 00:31:11.411
If your host
leaves these walls. it burns.

434
00:31:13.121 --> 00:31:16.166
Aemond has fled
and Rhaenyra holds my sister hostage.

435
00:31:17.167 --> 00:31:19.294
The River army
draws closer by the day.

436
00:31:19.336 --> 00:31:21.463
[knocking on table]
What possible course is there?

437
00:31:21.505 --> 00:31:24.341
Your uncle lacks imagination
as well as courage.

438
00:31:27.344 --> 00:31:29.638
I would take one Hightower sword

439
00:31:29.679 --> 00:31:31.598
over three of Tully's mudmen.

440
00:31:33.642 --> 00:31:35.185
When the usurper's host
comes here.

441
00:31:35.227 --> 00:31:37.396
we will fight on our terms.
on our ground.

442
00:31:40.357 --> 00:31:42.192
We have the clear advantage.

443
00:31:43.360 --> 00:31:45.362
Meanwhile. we are turning
King's Landing

444
00:31:45.404 --> 00:31:47.155
against that overweening cunt.

445
00:31:47.197 --> 00:31:49.699
little by little. bite by bite.

446
00:31:50.951 --> 00:31:53.703
Exposing her as weak
and unsuited to rule.

447
00:31:55.205 --> 00:31:57.374
The great houses cannot
but come to our side.

448
00:31:58.458 --> 00:31:59.876
Have any yet come?

449
00:32:01.920 --> 00:32:04.714
The patient hunter
gets the kill.

450
00:32:07.342 --> 00:32:09.886
Something the craven among us
would do well to learn.

451
00:32:12.222 --> 00:32:15.934
I have marched a long road.
fought and killed.

452
00:32:15.976 --> 00:32:18.687
and suffered my comrades
to be killed about me.

453
00:32:18.728 --> 00:32:20.272
Yes. you have endured much.

454
00:32:22.107 --> 00:32:25.986
I'm sure you found solace with
some of your brothers in arms.

455
00:32:27.070 --> 00:32:29.197
I am fatigued.

456
00:32:29.239 --> 00:32:31.575
It's been weeks
since I've seen a feather bed.

457
00:32:32.576 --> 00:32:34.202
By your leave.

458
00:32:34.244 --> 00:32:37.205
You might see Ser Gwayne
to his quarters. Your Grace.

459
00:32:37.247 --> 00:32:38.748
Make sure he bathes.

460
00:32:43.920 --> 00:32:45.755
Oh. and. uh...

461
00:32:46.965 --> 00:32:48.005
[whispering]
Mind yourself.

462
00:32:49.092 --> 00:32:51.094
Backs against the wall.

463
00:32:54.431 --> 00:32:57.267
-"Your Grace"?
-I'm sorry. I had to get through it.

464
00:32:57.309 --> 00:32:59.811
And this is your way?
Fawning?

465
00:32:59.853 --> 00:33:01.229
Daeron.

466
00:33:01.271 --> 00:33:03.315
He's styled you the bloody king.

467
00:33:03.356 --> 00:33:05.442
You left me alone with him.

468
00:33:05.484 --> 00:33:07.110
You know what he is.

469
00:33:07.152 --> 00:33:08.820
I do what I can
to keep him from...

470
00:33:10.030 --> 00:33:11.031
you know.

471
00:33:12.032 --> 00:33:13.742
I had no choice.

472
00:33:13.783 --> 00:33:15.242
No.

473
00:33:15.243 --> 00:33:17.454
But neither did it grieve you
to ride away.

474
00:33:21.124 --> 00:33:23.668
I hate what I am
when I'm with him.

475
00:33:23.710 --> 00:33:26.754
A puppet. a fool. a child.

476
00:33:26.755 --> 00:33:29.299
And yet he means
to put you on the throne. apparently.

477
00:33:30.634 --> 00:33:33.094
Only as he cannot
sit on it himself.

478
00:33:33.136 --> 00:33:35.764
No. he would thrust me forward
and devour me from within

479
00:33:35.805 --> 00:33:37.432
until there's nothing left.

480
00:33:37.474 --> 00:33:39.601
So tell him you won't do it.

481
00:33:39.643 --> 00:33:41.144
Then who will protect me then?

482
00:33:42.479 --> 00:33:45.315
Will you raise an army
against his savages?

483
00:33:48.652 --> 00:33:51.655
If you were king.
you could cast him down.

484
00:33:51.696 --> 00:33:54.324
I will never be king. uncle.
we both know it.

485
00:33:56.243 --> 00:33:58.453
[sighs] I need to lie down.

486
00:33:58.495 --> 00:34:00.497
-You'll stay. won't you?
-And do what?

487
00:34:01.790 --> 00:34:05.210
Bear witness whilst Ormund
marches our house to its doom?

488
00:34:07.003 --> 00:34:09.798
I'm second in line.
I shall return to Oldtown

489
00:34:09.839 --> 00:34:11.716
and prepare to pick up
the pieces.

490
00:34:11.758 --> 00:34:14.970
Don't leave me again.
Please.

491
00:34:15.011 --> 00:34:17.305
You're his little treasure now.

492
00:34:17.347 --> 00:34:18.682
You'll be fine.

493
00:34:21.184 --> 00:34:23.103
When you were in
King's Landing...

494
00:34:28.191 --> 00:34:29.693
Did you see my mother?

495
00:34:34.614 --> 00:34:36.408
[Alicent] Will you not eat?

496
00:34:40.412 --> 00:34:42.038
You have taken nothing
since yesterday

497
00:34:42.080 --> 00:34:43.623
and said little more.

498
00:34:50.589 --> 00:34:51.923
[softly] Helaena.

499
00:34:54.926 --> 00:34:57.178
Mysaria knew of our plan.

500
00:34:57.220 --> 00:34:59.139
but she said nothing
of Jaehaera.

501
00:35:01.266 --> 00:35:03.852
Was she truly stolen away
to meet us

502
00:35:03.893 --> 00:35:06.896
at some secret place up ahead?

503
00:35:13.361 --> 00:35:14.571
I see.

504
00:35:17.157 --> 00:35:18.783
Forgive me. Helaena.

505
00:35:18.825 --> 00:35:22.203
The... the road ahead
was fraught with peril.

506
00:35:22.245 --> 00:35:23.765
-To bring a small child...
-You lied.

507
00:35:26.583 --> 00:35:28.752
I wished only to save you
from this place.

508
00:35:29.753 --> 00:35:30.920
Me?

509
00:35:32.464 --> 00:35:33.757
Or yourself?

510
00:35:36.426 --> 00:35:38.094
What difference does it make?

511
00:35:40.430 --> 00:35:43.850
I have come too far.
I have sacrificed too much.

512
00:35:45.560 --> 00:35:47.979
If I cannot at long last
salvage my daughter...

513
00:35:57.781 --> 00:35:59.282
Helaena. please.

514
00:36:01.785 --> 00:36:03.119
Please. you must eat.

515
00:36:07.123 --> 00:36:10.126
[♪ somber music playing]

516
00:36:26.851 --> 00:36:28.478
[horse neighing]

517
00:36:37.737 --> 00:36:38.863
[softly] One-Eye.

518
00:36:41.574 --> 00:36:43.159
-[blade stabbing]
-[gasps]

519
00:36:48.415 --> 00:36:49.833
I have kept your secret.

520
00:36:51.042 --> 00:36:52.794
I will keep it still.

521
00:36:52.836 --> 00:36:54.421
You could have killed me. too.

522
00:36:55.547 --> 00:36:57.006
And claimed Rhaenyra's bounty.

523
00:36:58.091 --> 00:37:00.218
There are many things
I could have done to you.

524
00:37:02.011 --> 00:37:03.847
Then what is this game you play?

525
00:37:05.515 --> 00:37:07.016
It's yours to learn.

526
00:37:08.393 --> 00:37:10.019
If your spirit is willing.

527
00:37:12.021 --> 00:37:14.524
[chest dragging]

528
00:37:29.581 --> 00:37:31.374
Have you forgotten your history?

529
00:37:33.042 --> 00:37:34.502
Dreamfyre.

530
00:37:34.544 --> 00:37:37.005
Your ancestor

531
00:37:37.046 --> 00:37:39.007
Rhaena Targaryen
came to Harrenhal

532
00:37:39.048 --> 00:37:41.092
after the death of her daughter.

533
00:37:42.218 --> 00:37:45.221
And she grieved
and grew old here.

534
00:37:46.097 --> 00:37:48.933
Her dragon laid a clutch of eggs
before Rhaena herself died.

535
00:37:48.975 --> 00:37:51.186
and they have sat here.

536
00:37:51.227 --> 00:37:53.605
cold and abandoned
these hundred years.

537
00:37:55.356 --> 00:37:57.275
I do not know
the ways of dragons.

538
00:37:57.317 --> 00:38:01.070
but I have long envisaged
the return of the Targaryens

539
00:38:01.112 --> 00:38:03.615
to this ancient seat.

540
00:38:03.656 --> 00:38:05.658
[rain falling]

541
00:38:10.789 --> 00:38:12.582
I have been cursed for my sins.

542
00:38:13.750 --> 00:38:14.834
Alys.

543
00:38:16.419 --> 00:38:19.088
All I put my hand to
withers beneath its touch.

544
00:38:20.340 --> 00:38:24.260
Do you imagine that you alone
know what it is to be cursed?

545
00:38:27.597 --> 00:38:30.642
I'm tired of this
desolate existence.

546
00:38:32.477 --> 00:38:34.479
And so. I think. are you.

547
00:38:36.272 --> 00:38:38.316
[thunder rumbling]

548
00:38:38.358 --> 00:38:41.152
You've been alone
your whole life. Aemond.

549
00:38:43.321 --> 00:38:45.615
Can you not imagine...

550
00:38:46.825 --> 00:38:48.284
what it would be...

551
00:38:49.953 --> 00:38:52.163
to have it otherwise?

552
00:39:00.296 --> 00:39:01.673
[Aemond] It's warm.

553
00:39:07.178 --> 00:39:09.389
There's an ancient
strength here.

554
00:39:11.140 --> 00:39:13.476
Let the gods turn
their backs on us.

555
00:39:13.518 --> 00:39:15.812
We will make our own fortune.

556
00:39:18.731 --> 00:39:20.650
I will be the Lady of the Water.

557
00:39:21.818 --> 00:39:23.444
[sighs]

558
00:39:23.486 --> 00:39:24.696
And you...

559
00:39:27.198 --> 00:39:30.869
the dragonlord by my side.

560
00:39:35.665 --> 00:39:38.376
But in the meantime.
you're a Targaryen prince.

561
00:39:40.670 --> 00:39:42.963
And your sons

562
00:39:42.964 --> 00:39:46.801
will be Targaryen princes
in their turn.

563
00:39:46.843 --> 00:39:48.845
♪♪

564
00:39:54.100 --> 00:39:56.644
[baby crying]

565
00:39:56.686 --> 00:39:59.230
Tallow is scarce
and cost thrice what it did.

566
00:39:59.272 --> 00:40:00.982
We cannot light our sconces.

567
00:40:01.024 --> 00:40:02.483
You know my response.

568
00:40:02.525 --> 00:40:04.903
Ser Torrhen Manderly
is Master of Coin.

569
00:40:04.944 --> 00:40:08.990
It is his task now to distribute
what resources we have.

570
00:40:09.032 --> 00:40:11.367
I suggest you address
Ser Torrhen himself.

571
00:40:12.535 --> 00:40:14.037
Bring the next.

572
00:40:15.538 --> 00:40:17.665
Your Grace.

573
00:40:17.707 --> 00:40:21.002
The motherhouse
lately enjoyed the protection

574
00:40:21.044 --> 00:40:22.712
of the City Watch.

575
00:40:23.963 --> 00:40:26.132
Now. we are in peril.

576
00:40:26.966 --> 00:40:31.262
One of our girls
only last night was taken.

577
00:40:32.263 --> 00:40:34.265
You have my condolences.
I shall...

578
00:40:36.392 --> 00:40:39.020
light a candle for her
when next I attend the sept.

579
00:40:39.062 --> 00:40:41.064
[crowd murmuring]

580
00:40:42.732 --> 00:40:45.109
Godric. Your Grace.
A mason.

581
00:40:45.151 --> 00:40:47.195
We have watched in fear
as we found gold cloaks

582
00:40:47.236 --> 00:40:49.030
murdered among us.
and I have heard

583
00:40:49.072 --> 00:40:51.449
a great number of 'em
have resigned their posts.

584
00:40:51.491 --> 00:40:52.951
leaving the streets undefended.

585
00:40:52.992 --> 00:40:55.870
Yes. these are Hightower crimes.

586
00:40:55.912 --> 00:40:58.122
The craven Ormund strikes at me
from Tumbleton.

587
00:40:58.164 --> 00:41:00.959
where he has concealed himself
among innocents.

588
00:41:01.000 --> 00:41:02.126
[Godric] This we know.

589
00:41:02.168 --> 00:41:03.920
But how will we now
be protected?

590
00:41:03.962 --> 00:41:06.589
If the City Watch fails.
then who will preserve order among us?

591
00:41:06.631 --> 00:41:08.549
I have sent for Velaryon men

592
00:41:08.591 --> 00:41:10.611
-to root out the enemy within our walls.
-[crowd clamoring]

593
00:41:10.635 --> 00:41:12.237
Once they arrive.
the city shall be returned...

594
00:41:12.261 --> 00:41:13.930
[townsperson]
How will they be protected?

595
00:41:13.972 --> 00:41:16.975
-[clamoring continues]
-[septa] She was but six and 10!

596
00:41:18.810 --> 00:41:21.562
[Godric]
Your Grace. we are afraid.

597
00:41:21.604 --> 00:41:23.147
And wherever the fault lies.

598
00:41:23.189 --> 00:41:25.650
we have none
to look to now but you.

599
00:41:25.692 --> 00:41:28.695
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

600
00:41:34.534 --> 00:41:36.828
[crowd continues clamoring]

601
00:41:45.461 --> 00:41:47.463
[clamoring continues]

602
00:41:48.673 --> 00:41:50.675
[people chattering]

603
00:42:04.063 --> 00:42:06.065
[chattering continues]

604
00:42:28.254 --> 00:42:29.672
Daemon Targaryen.

605
00:42:31.007 --> 00:42:32.842
How many?

606
00:42:32.884 --> 00:42:35.636
How many of you are there?

607
00:42:35.678 --> 00:42:38.222
-How many?!
-We have no number.

608
00:42:38.264 --> 00:42:40.058
We are everywhere.

609
00:42:43.728 --> 00:42:45.646
What did Ormund Hightower
promise you. gold?

610
00:42:45.688 --> 00:42:46.898
Huh?

611
00:42:46.939 --> 00:42:48.815
A place at his table
when he takes the throne?

612
00:42:48.816 --> 00:42:52.070
There is a king waiting
just outside these walls.

613
00:42:52.111 --> 00:42:54.238
And until Daeron the Daring
takes his rightful place.

614
00:42:54.280 --> 00:42:55.740
we will not rest.

615
00:42:55.782 --> 00:42:57.992
Then your kind
will die in dragonfire.

616
00:42:58.034 --> 00:43:00.870
or trampled down by my army.

617
00:43:00.912 --> 00:43:03.247
Will she lay waste
to her own city?

618
00:43:03.289 --> 00:43:05.750
Will she set upon her own people
with swords?

619
00:43:05.792 --> 00:43:07.001
You'll never find us.

620
00:43:07.043 --> 00:43:08.562
We're the people
of the Seven Kingdoms.

621
00:43:08.586 --> 00:43:11.839
We have no sign or sigil.
And when you strike us.

622
00:43:11.881 --> 00:43:14.717
you only drive more
to our cause.

623
00:43:16.636 --> 00:43:18.221
You rebel against one

624
00:43:18.262 --> 00:43:20.139
who has neither wished
nor done you harm.

625
00:43:21.224 --> 00:43:24.102
You can burn us.
You can kill us.

626
00:43:24.143 --> 00:43:26.062
You will never make us
embrace her.

627
00:43:29.774 --> 00:43:31.234
[groans]

628
00:43:47.083 --> 00:43:48.251
Watch where you're fucking...

629
00:43:49.794 --> 00:43:50.920
Your prince.

630
00:43:51.838 --> 00:43:53.172
Uh. Your Grace.

631
00:43:54.090 --> 00:43:55.716
What is your errand here?

632
00:43:55.758 --> 00:43:58.136
I... I was... I thought...

633
00:43:59.095 --> 00:44:01.430
I... I was just...

634
00:44:02.181 --> 00:44:03.641
I'm taking the air.

635
00:44:03.683 --> 00:44:06.269
Are you not commanded to stay
in the Keep under guard?

636
00:44:08.938 --> 00:44:10.106
Well. yes.

637
00:44:11.440 --> 00:44:13.568
In a manner of speaking.

638
00:44:13.609 --> 00:44:15.111
Insolent maggot.

639
00:44:15.820 --> 00:44:18.447
I'm up that bloody hill
for days at a time.

640
00:44:19.532 --> 00:44:21.617
Men deserve
their simple pleasures.

641
00:44:22.827 --> 00:44:24.203
Keep us going.

642
00:44:25.454 --> 00:44:27.081
You yourself should understand...

643
00:44:27.123 --> 00:44:29.041
-[grunting]
-[crowd gasps]

644
00:44:30.835 --> 00:44:33.671
-[groaning]
-Set foot in the city again.

645
00:44:33.713 --> 00:44:35.631
and I'll put out your eyes.

646
00:44:37.633 --> 00:44:40.636
[♪ dramatic music playing]

647
00:44:54.025 --> 00:44:56.027
[chatter resumes]

648
00:45:01.991 --> 00:45:03.993
[hoofbeats approaching]

649
00:45:05.161 --> 00:45:06.829
[horse neighing]

650
00:45:22.678 --> 00:45:24.263
Ho. there.

651
00:45:25.014 --> 00:45:26.766
Ho. Friend.

652
00:45:34.690 --> 00:45:37.276
[soldier] Come on!
Put your backs into it!

653
00:45:38.861 --> 00:45:40.696
[indistinct shouting]
Come on!

654
00:45:42.740 --> 00:45:44.659
[soldiers chattering]

655
00:45:44.700 --> 00:45:45.785
All clear!

656
00:45:47.411 --> 00:45:48.871
Here.

657
00:45:59.131 --> 00:46:01.259
[Ormund]
<i>The common man is. as a rule.</i>

658
00:46:01.300 --> 00:46:03.552
<i>of no interest or concern.</i>

659
00:46:03.594 --> 00:46:07.223
<i>But you must never trust one
who's clawed his way to power.</i>

660
00:46:07.265 --> 00:46:10.434
His ambition is oft fueled
by some lack.

661
00:46:11.394 --> 00:46:14.814
Some shame. or lust. or rage.

662
00:46:16.565 --> 00:46:17.900
Mm.

663
00:46:17.942 --> 00:46:20.361
You should think on it
when you choose your Hand.

664
00:46:20.403 --> 00:46:23.406
Rhaenyra made a rare good choice
with Corlys Velaryon.

665
00:46:24.407 --> 00:46:26.534
There is a soundness
to his breeding.

666
00:46:26.575 --> 00:46:29.161
Not the sordid appetite
of the striver.

667
00:46:30.454 --> 00:46:31.914
What of my grandsire?

668
00:46:33.416 --> 00:46:35.042
Otto? [chuckles]

669
00:46:35.084 --> 00:46:36.627
Where do I begin?

670
00:46:36.669 --> 00:46:39.547
My lord. House Baratheon
sends an envoy

671
00:46:39.588 --> 00:46:41.424
to treat with the new king.

672
00:46:43.551 --> 00:46:46.053
Let the Stormlands lead the way.

673
00:46:46.095 --> 00:46:48.139
Highgarden will have no choice
but to follow.

674
00:46:49.640 --> 00:46:51.392
[sighs] Stand up.

675
00:46:51.434 --> 00:46:52.643
Stand up. both of you!

676
00:46:55.104 --> 00:46:58.899
Lord Ormund Hightower.
Beacon of the South.

677
00:46:58.941 --> 00:47:04.030
Defender of the Citadel.
and Voice of Oldtown.

678
00:47:07.158 --> 00:47:08.784
Well met. Ser Ormund.

679
00:47:09.660 --> 00:47:12.330
I come as an envoy
of Lord Borros Baratheon.

680
00:47:12.371 --> 00:47:14.582
Lord Paramount
of the Stormlands.

681
00:47:14.623 --> 00:47:16.417
Mm.

682
00:47:16.459 --> 00:47:17.710
[clearing throat]

683
00:47:19.295 --> 00:47:22.631
-You are quite welcome. Ser...
-Ser Arrion Baratheon.

684
00:47:22.673 --> 00:47:24.717
Cousin to Lord Borros.

685
00:47:28.888 --> 00:47:31.932
I most regret presenting
ourselves to you in this state.

686
00:47:31.974 --> 00:47:33.851
The road was long and filthy.

687
00:47:33.893 --> 00:47:36.479
but I thought it best
to speak to you immediately.

688
00:47:36.520 --> 00:47:37.813
We are honored to receive you.

689
00:47:38.731 --> 00:47:40.775
And what word from Lord Borros?

690
00:47:40.816 --> 00:47:43.277
Well. House Baratheon
bends the knee to His Grace.

691
00:47:43.319 --> 00:47:45.821
King Daeron Targaryen.
and offers its many banners

692
00:47:45.863 --> 00:47:47.656
in alliance
with House Hightower.

693
00:47:49.700 --> 00:47:51.785
I have been ordered
to swear fealty

694
00:47:51.786 --> 00:47:54.080
to the new king
on behalf of Lord Borros.

695
00:47:55.706 --> 00:47:58.209
Your lord has made
a wise choice.

696
00:48:01.420 --> 00:48:03.506
If we might see
the king in person.

697
00:48:03.547 --> 00:48:05.508
that we may bend the knee
before him.

698
00:48:08.844 --> 00:48:11.430
His Grace. Daeron Targaryen.

699
00:48:13.682 --> 00:48:15.101
The First of his Name.

700
00:48:17.186 --> 00:48:20.481
King of the Andals.
the Rhoynar and the...

701
00:48:20.523 --> 00:48:22.483
-[blade slashing]
-No! Stop him!

702
00:48:22.525 --> 00:48:23.859
-[men shouting]
-Stop him!

703
00:48:23.901 --> 00:48:25.361
-Stop him!
-No!

704
00:48:26.695 --> 00:48:28.322
These are assassins.

705
00:48:28.364 --> 00:48:30.324
sent for Daeron and you.

706
00:48:30.366 --> 00:48:32.118
-[flesh squelching]
-[grunting]

707
00:48:33.911 --> 00:48:35.204
[splatting]

708
00:48:36.872 --> 00:48:39.542
-[swords clanging]
-[men shouting]

709
00:48:41.710 --> 00:48:43.462
[grunting]

710
00:48:45.589 --> 00:48:49.677
Ser Arrion Baratheon
has hair of light chestnut.

711
00:48:49.718 --> 00:48:52.513
He's about a foot taller.
and as it happens...

712
00:48:52.555 --> 00:48:54.390
-[blood streaming]
-far more comely.

713
00:48:54.432 --> 00:48:55.433
[thud]

714
00:48:59.145 --> 00:49:02.440
I will cleave the bitch
from crown to cunt.

715
00:49:03.399 --> 00:49:05.401
She will die
wishing she never dared...

716
00:49:07.736 --> 00:49:08.779
Dared...

717
00:49:08.821 --> 00:49:10.823
[retching]

718
00:49:19.498 --> 00:49:20.499
Kat.

719
00:49:26.172 --> 00:49:27.673
[sighs]

720
00:49:34.638 --> 00:49:36.682
I thought you were d-dead.

721
00:49:38.517 --> 00:49:39.768
[Kat whimpering]

722
00:49:45.274 --> 00:49:47.276
[sobbing]

723
00:49:50.279 --> 00:49:52.114
I looked for you.

724
00:49:52.156 --> 00:49:53.991
I went home. but you'd gone.

725
00:49:54.033 --> 00:49:55.951
What choice did I have?

726
00:49:57.495 --> 00:49:58.704
I was alone.

727
00:50:00.164 --> 00:50:03.125
I escaped in the chaos.
I came here to my brother.

728
00:50:04.126 --> 00:50:05.711
And now. he's dead. too.

729
00:50:08.380 --> 00:50:10.049
But Kat. I've done it.

730
00:50:11.050 --> 00:50:12.801
I claimed a dragon.

731
00:50:13.636 --> 00:50:15.930
Vermithor. the Bronze Fury.

732
00:50:15.971 --> 00:50:17.640
I've been made a knight.

733
00:50:18.641 --> 00:50:20.476
And the queen has promised...

734
00:50:25.022 --> 00:50:26.649
Is that what this is?

735
00:50:28.025 --> 00:50:29.693
Dragon?

736
00:50:32.321 --> 00:50:35.115
-You smell different.
-We'll have coin now.

737
00:50:35.157 --> 00:50:36.992
A fine house. anything you wish.

738
00:50:37.910 --> 00:50:40.120
I can take you
out of this to safety.

739
00:50:40.162 --> 00:50:41.455
Do you not see?

740
00:50:41.497 --> 00:50:44.208
Your husband is a dragonrider.

741
00:50:45.209 --> 00:50:46.919
Do you know
how many days it takes...

742
00:50:48.212 --> 00:50:50.548
to walk the road here
from King's Landing?

743
00:50:53.384 --> 00:50:57.972
Do you know what may befall
a woman alone on that road?

744
00:50:58.013 --> 00:50:59.723
Did something happen?

745
00:51:01.267 --> 00:51:02.893
Many things happened.

746
00:51:05.062 --> 00:51:08.399
While you were on Dragonstone...

747
00:51:09.441 --> 00:51:11.819
-seeking out your own glory.
-I did it for you.

748
00:51:11.860 --> 00:51:13.279
I didn't want it!

749
00:51:15.197 --> 00:51:18.409
I needed you here.

750
00:51:19.535 --> 00:51:21.120
On the ground.

751
00:51:25.791 --> 00:51:27.918
[whispering] I'm sorry. I am.

752
00:51:27.960 --> 00:51:29.878
But I... I can stay no longer.

753
00:51:29.920 --> 00:51:31.672
If I am discovered here...

754
00:51:31.714 --> 00:51:33.299
Just come with me.

755
00:51:34.592 --> 00:51:36.552
I won't forsake my family.

756
00:51:38.804 --> 00:51:40.198
There is no time.
Come. we're going.

757
00:51:40.222 --> 00:51:42.766
-No!
-I will not leave you in peril.

758
00:51:42.808 --> 00:51:44.119
-What are you doing?
-[shushing]

759
00:51:44.143 --> 00:51:45.894
[muffled shouting]

760
00:51:46.937 --> 00:51:48.230
Who are you?!

761
00:51:49.607 --> 00:51:51.609
[whimpering]

762
00:51:56.655 --> 00:51:58.657
[breathing heavily]

763
00:52:03.579 --> 00:52:05.581
-[people shouting]
-[swords clanging]

764
00:52:20.095 --> 00:52:21.722
[Ormund] You did well.

765
00:52:21.764 --> 00:52:25.100
I treated you harshly.
and for that. I'm sorry.

766
00:52:26.477 --> 00:52:28.312
The strains of the campaign.

767
00:52:32.024 --> 00:52:34.777
You may return to Oldtown
if you wish.

768
00:52:34.818 --> 00:52:37.298
A small band of men
won't attract the attention of the dragons.

769
00:52:38.656 --> 00:52:40.592
-I'll not stop you.
-[Daeron] There are three of you.

770
00:52:40.616 --> 00:52:42.743
Should be easy.
Again.

771
00:52:42.785 --> 00:52:44.787
[shouting. clanging resumes]

772
00:52:44.828 --> 00:52:46.372
[Gwayne]
He'd make a good king.

773
00:52:48.374 --> 00:52:49.958
Not that that matters to you.

774
00:52:54.213 --> 00:52:56.715
You think me so callous.

775
00:52:57.633 --> 00:53:01.011
I think you'd sacrifice lives
to feed your own pride.

776
00:53:03.639 --> 00:53:05.849
But I know you'd never
sacrifice your own.

777
00:53:09.144 --> 00:53:10.396
So. tell me.

778
00:53:12.648 --> 00:53:13.982
What is your plan here?

779
00:53:18.070 --> 00:53:19.488
Speak your purpose.

780
00:53:21.156 --> 00:53:22.157
Helaena.

781
00:53:23.325 --> 00:53:24.827
She cannot stay confined.

782
00:53:26.203 --> 00:53:28.956
Her state of mind is precarious.
her condition being what it is.

783
00:53:28.997 --> 00:53:31.583
Do you have something useful
for me. or have I been misled?

784
00:53:35.003 --> 00:53:36.505
I know where Aemond is.

785
00:53:39.258 --> 00:53:41.844
-All this time?
-O-Only... only lately.

786
00:53:44.763 --> 00:53:47.224
I would need a guarantee
that we'd go free.

787
00:53:48.100 --> 00:53:49.518
Both of us.
as originally agreed.

788
00:53:49.560 --> 00:53:52.354
You're in no place to demand
guarantees of anything.

789
00:53:52.396 --> 00:53:54.440
When Aemond is gone.
your reign is assured.

790
00:53:55.941 --> 00:53:57.151
Ormund will surrender or die.

791
00:53:57.192 --> 00:53:58.736
Helaena and I
are no threat to you.

792
00:53:58.777 --> 00:54:01.071
We will disappear.
You will not hear of us again.

793
00:54:07.077 --> 00:54:08.704
Where is he?

794
00:54:09.747 --> 00:54:10.914
Harrenhal.

795
00:54:11.957 --> 00:54:14.501
My riders have searched
for Vhagar there

796
00:54:14.543 --> 00:54:17.463
-half a dozen times.
-I did not say I know where Vhagar is.

797
00:54:20.966 --> 00:54:22.718
How did you come by this?

798
00:54:24.553 --> 00:54:26.054
There are times when Helaena...

799
00:54:26.972 --> 00:54:28.599
when Helaena sees things.

800
00:54:29.433 --> 00:54:31.185
It will sound mad.

801
00:54:31.226 --> 00:54:33.771
They are nightmares
or... or puzzles.

802
00:54:35.939 --> 00:54:38.817
But the things she does see
now and then. they come to pass.

803
00:54:40.986 --> 00:54:42.446
She dreams.

804
00:54:44.573 --> 00:54:46.241
She's a dreamer.

805
00:54:48.076 --> 00:54:49.745
Like Daenys
who foresaw the Doom.

806
00:54:56.126 --> 00:54:58.253
If what you say is true.

807
00:54:58.295 --> 00:55:01.590
if Aemond has separated
somehow from his dragon...

808
00:55:03.509 --> 00:55:04.635
then...

809
00:55:06.178 --> 00:55:08.305
he is one man on foot...

810
00:55:09.807 --> 00:55:11.141
and being hunted.

811
00:55:13.435 --> 00:55:15.562
He will have hidden himself
so he cannot be found.

812
00:55:15.604 --> 00:55:17.063
I have told you all that I know.

813
00:55:17.064 --> 00:55:19.566
His capture must now
fall to you and your council.

814
00:55:19.608 --> 00:55:20.609
No.

815
00:55:24.780 --> 00:55:27.199
If I send swords...

816
00:55:29.326 --> 00:55:31.286
he will flee again.
go to ground.

817
00:55:31.328 --> 00:55:32.621
and be lost. but...

818
00:55:38.377 --> 00:55:40.003
If I send just one sword...

819
00:55:45.884 --> 00:55:47.678
with someone he trusts...

820
00:55:56.061 --> 00:55:57.855
No. I will...
I will be no part of this.

821
00:56:00.399 --> 00:56:03.485
-No. please. Rhaenyra.
-Unhand her Grace.

822
00:56:07.364 --> 00:56:08.490
I...

823
00:56:09.366 --> 00:56:11.910
I... I cannot leave Helaena.

824
00:56:18.750 --> 00:56:20.252
I will keep watch over her.

825
00:56:21.503 --> 00:56:22.921
Until you return.

826
00:56:28.886 --> 00:56:30.178
Did I not warn you...

827
00:56:31.597 --> 00:56:33.015
that you would come to this?

828
00:56:53.869 --> 00:56:55.370
I don't want to be alone.

829
00:56:56.788 --> 00:56:59.041
[sighs] Nor do I.

830
00:57:01.251 --> 00:57:02.544
I have no choice.

831
00:57:07.132 --> 00:57:08.133
Here.

832
00:57:09.426 --> 00:57:11.136
You could refuse.

833
00:57:15.182 --> 00:57:16.892
And Aemond would
still be like to die.

834
00:57:19.061 --> 00:57:21.146
Do you not wish to be free?

835
00:57:24.399 --> 00:57:25.734
Why am I here?

836
00:57:29.154 --> 00:57:31.740
Was there no other lord
that offered for my hand?

837
00:57:35.577 --> 00:57:39.414
Or was it your own desire

838
00:57:39.456 --> 00:57:41.458
to marry me to my brother?

839
00:57:48.757 --> 00:57:50.425
It was my father's wish.

840
00:57:53.428 --> 00:57:54.930
But I did not begrudge it.

841
00:57:57.432 --> 00:58:01.436
Better here with me. I thought.
than a man you did not know

842
00:58:01.478 --> 00:58:03.855
in a place far away.

843
00:58:13.448 --> 00:58:15.951
Please. Please.

844
00:58:19.413 --> 00:58:23.625
We still have some
small chance at freedom. Helaena.

845
00:58:25.460 --> 00:58:27.796
But I cannot go unless I know
you are sustained.

846
00:58:29.297 --> 00:58:31.258
[sighs]

847
00:58:31.299 --> 00:58:32.300
Please.

848
00:58:45.981 --> 00:58:47.232
[softly] There.

849
00:58:50.318 --> 00:58:53.655
I will return to you
as soon as I am able.

850
00:58:53.697 --> 00:58:55.490
I give you my word.

851
00:58:55.532 --> 00:58:58.326
I will come back
and collect you. and we will...

852
00:58:59.244 --> 00:59:01.163
we will walk out in the sun.

853
00:59:03.665 --> 00:59:06.668
[♪ soft. dramatic music playing]

854
00:59:30.025 --> 00:59:31.860
[Orwyle]
Forgive the hour. Your Grace.

855
00:59:34.571 --> 00:59:38.575
There has been a rider
from Tumbleton.

856
00:59:47.084 --> 00:59:48.710
"Kick this dog...

857
00:59:49.878 --> 00:59:52.047
and it will bite your hand."

858
00:59:54.716 --> 00:59:56.718
[soldiers singing indistinctly]

859
00:59:59.554 --> 01:00:02.390
[Corlys]
<i>You have fought like sharks.</i>

860
01:00:03.725 --> 01:00:06.061
<i>Swift and relentless.</i>

861
01:00:07.604 --> 01:00:10.190
We have cut through our enemy

862
01:00:10.232 --> 01:00:12.901
-and routed them!
-[soldiers cheering]

863
01:00:14.569 --> 01:00:18.240
But now. your blades
are needed in the city.

864
01:00:21.743 --> 01:00:23.078
And I...

865
01:00:24.663 --> 01:00:26.540
I have been too long away.

866
01:00:26.581 --> 01:00:29.584
[♪ dramatic music playing]

867
01:00:39.928 --> 01:00:41.096
Who are you?

868
01:00:42.472 --> 01:00:44.015
What's your errand?

869
01:00:46.309 --> 01:00:48.311
[Corlys grunting]

870
01:00:50.147 --> 01:00:52.607
[soldiers shouting]

871
01:00:54.484 --> 01:00:56.570
[shouting continues]

872
01:00:56.611 --> 01:00:59.614
[♪ dramatic music intensifying]

873
01:01:05.954 --> 01:01:07.956
♪♪

873
01:01:08.305 --> 01:02:08.175
Do you want subtitles for any video?
